G112.b:
* ⟪ἄ-θεος⟫, -ον,
⟪1.⟫ in cl.
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪slighting⟫ or ⟪denying the gods⟫ (Plat.; cf. MM, VGT, s.v.);
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪godless, ungodly⟫ (Pind.);
	⟪(c)⟫ ⟪abandoned by the gods⟫ (Soph.)
⟪2.⟫ In the NT (cf. Lft. on Ign. ad Trail, §3), of the heathen, ⟪without God, not knowing God⟫ (Cremer, 281): ⟦Ephesians 2:12|Eph 2:12⟧.†

G129.b:
⟪αἷμα⟫, ατος, τό,
[in LXX for ⁨דָּם⁩;] ⟪blood.⟫
⟪1.⟫ In the ordinary sense: ⟦Mark 5:25|Mk 5:25⟧, ⟦Luke 8:43|Lk 8:43⟧, ⟦Luke 8:44|44⟧ ⟦Luke 22:44|22:44⟧, ⟦John 19:34|Jo 19:34⟧, ⟦Acts 15:20|Ac 15:20⟧, ⟦Acts 15:29|29⟧ ⟦Acts 21:25|21:25⟧, ⟦Revelation 8:7|Re 8:7⟧, ⟦Revelation 8:8|8⟧ ⟦Revelation 11:6|11:6⟧ ⟦Revelation 16:3|16:3⟧, ⟦Revelation 16:4|4⟧, ⟦Revelation 16:6|6⟧ ⟦Revelation 19:13|19:13⟧.
⟪2.⟫ In special senses:
	⟪(a)⟫ of generation, origin, kinship (cl.): ⟦John 1:13|Jo 1:13⟧ (v. MM, VGT, s.v.);
	⟪(b)⟫ as in OT (AR on ⟦Ephesians 6:12|Eph, 6:12⟧), in the phrase σάρξ καὶ αἷ. (αἷ. κ. σ.), to indicate human nature as opp. to God and created spirits: ⟦Matthew 16:17|Mt 16:17⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:50|I Co 15:50⟧, ⟦Galatians 1:16|Ga 1:16⟧, ⟦Ephesians 6:12|Eph 6:12⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:14|He 2:14⟧;
	⟪(c)⟫ of things in colour resembling blood: ⟦Acts 2:19|Ac 2:19⟧, ⟦Acts 2:20|20⟧, ⟦Revelation 6:12|Re 6:12⟧ ⟦Revelation 14:18|14:18⟧-⟦Revelation 14:20|20⟧.
	⟪(d)⟫ of bloodshed, a bloody death (cl.): ⟦Matthew 23:30|Mt 23:30⟧, ⟦Matthew 23:35|35⟧ ⟦Matthew 27:4|27:4⟧, ⟦Matthew 27:6|6⟧, ⟦Matthew 27:8|8⟧, ⟦Matthew 27:24|24⟧, ⟦Matthew 27:25|25⟧, ⟦Luke 11:50|Lk 11:50⟧, ⟦Luke 11:51|51⟧ ⟦Luke 13:1|13:1⟧, ⟦Acts 1:19|Ac 1:19⟧ ⟦Acts 5:28|5:28⟧ ⟦Acts 18:6|18:6⟧ ⟦Acts 20:26|20:26⟧ ⟦Acts 22:20|22:20⟧, ⟦Hebrews 12:4|He 12:4⟧, ⟦Revelation 6:10|Re 6:10⟧ ⟦Revelation 17:6|17:6⟧ ⟦Revelation 18:24|18:24⟧ ⟦Revelation 19:2|19:2⟧ ; αἷ. ἐκχέειν (Deiss., LAE, 428; MM, VGT, s.v., αἷ.), ⟦Romans 3:15|Ro 3:15⟧, ⟦Revelation 16:6|Re 16:6⟧;
	⟪(e)⟫ of sacrificial blood, as an expiation: ⟦Hebrews 9:7|He 9:7⟧, ⟦Hebrews 9:12|12⟧, ⟦Hebrews 9:13|13⟧, ⟦Hebrews 9:18|18⟧-⟦Hebrews 9:22|22⟧, ⟦Hebrews 9:25|25⟧ ⟦Hebrews 10:4|10:4⟧ ⟦Hebrews 11:28|11:28⟧ ⟦Hebrews 13:11|13:11⟧; of the blood of Christ, ⟦Matthew 26:28|Mt 26:28⟧, ⟦Mark 14:24|Mk 14:24⟧, ⟦Luke 22:20|Lk 22:20⟧, ⟦John 6:53|Jo 6:53⟧, ⟦John 6:54|54⟧, ⟦John 6:56|56⟧, ⟦Acts 20:28|Ac 20:28⟧, ⟦Romans 3:25|Ro 3:25⟧ ⟦Romans 5:9|5:9⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 10:16|I Co 10:16⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 11:25|11:25⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 11:27|27⟧, ⟦Ephesians 1:7|Eph 1:7⟧ ⟦Ephesians 2:13|2:13⟧, ⟦Colossians 1:20|Col 1:20⟧, ⟦Hebrews 9:12|He 9:12⟧, ⟦Hebrews 9:14|14⟧ ⟦Hebrews 10:19|10:19⟧, ⟦Hebrews 10:29|29⟧ ⟦Hebrews 12:24|12:24⟧ ⟦Hebrews 13:20|13:20⟧, ⟦1 Peter 1:2|I Pe 1:2⟧, ⟦1 Peter 1:19|19⟧, ⟦1 John 1:7|I Jo 1:7⟧ (cf. ⟦1 John 5:6|5:6⟧, ⟦1 John 5:8|8⟧), ⟦Revelation 1:5|Re 1:5⟧ ⟦Revelation 5:9|5:9⟧ ⟦Revelation 7:14|7:14⟧ ⟦Revelation 12:11|12:11⟧. (Cremer, 69 f., 612 f.)†

G166.b:
⟪αἰώνιος⟫, -ον (as usual in Attic), also -α, -ον. ⟦2 Thessalonians 2:16|II Th 2:16⟧, ⟦Hebrews 9:12|He 9:12⟧;
(< αἰών), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨עוֹלָם⁩;] ⟪age-long⟫, ⟪eternal⟫,
⟪(a)⟫ of that which is without either beginning or end: ⟦Romans 16:26|Ro 16:26⟧, ⟦Hebrews 9:14|He 9:14⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of that which is without beginning: ⟦Romans 16:25|Ro 16:25⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 1:9|II Ti 1:9⟧, ⟦Titus 1:2|Tit 1:2⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ of that which is without end (MM, VGT, s.v.): σκηναί, ⟦Luke 16:9|Lk 16:9⟧ οἰκία, ⟦2 Corinthians 5:1|II Co 5:1⟧; διαθήκη, ⟦Hebrews 13:20|He 13:20⟧; εὐαγγέλιον, ⟦Revelation 14:6|Re 14:6⟧; παράκλησις, ⟦2 Thessalonians 2:16|II Th 2:16⟧; λύτρωσις, ⟦Hebrews 9:12|He 9:12⟧; κληρονομία, ⟦Hebrews 9:15|ib. 15⟧; κόλασις, ⟦Matthew 25:46|Mt 25:46⟧; κρίμα, ⟦Hebrews 6:2|He 6:2⟧; κρίσις, ⟦Mark 3:29|Mk 3:29⟧; ὄλεθρον, ⟦2 Thessalonians 1:9|II Th 1:9⟧; πῦρ, ⟦Matthew 18:8|Mt 18:8⟧; freq. c. ζωή, q.v.
SYN.: ἀΐδιος, q.v.

G169.b:
⟪ἀκάθαρτος⟫, -ον
(< ἀ- neg., καθαίρω), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨טָמֵא⁩;] ⟪unclean, impure⟫;
